P6 (issue #23, U16): give every surrogate new closed/maximal and
generator filters.

The item set reporter filters closed and maximal item sets with a
repository of the sets found so far (clomax) and generators with a hash
table of the generators found so far (gentab). The reporter is reused
for every surrogate and neither repository is reset, so later
surrogates are checked against the sets of earlier ones: closed and
maximal sets are lost (e.g. -gp -tm -s-2 on a 4-item data set from the
third surrogate on) and for generators the program crashes (SIGSEGV in
is_isgen, report.c, from the second surrogate on, e.g. -gr -tg -s-4 on
dense data). isr_settarg with the reporter's target and mode and the
direction of fpg_report (-1) deletes both and creates new ones. Extends
clrpex of P2b, which is called after every fpg_mine.

--- a/fpgrowth/src/fpgpsp.c
+++ b/fpgrowth/src/fpgpsp.c
@@ -208,7 +208,8 @@
   for (n = rep->pxpp[0] & ~ITEM_MIN; --n >= 0; )
     rep->pxpp[*rep->pexs++] &= ~ITEM_MIN;
   rep->pxpp[0] &= ITEM_MIN;     /* unmark the items, clear the count */
-}  /* clrpex() */
+  isr_settarg(rep, rep->target, rep->mode, -1); /* P6: new c/m and */
+}  /* clrpex() */                /* generator filters (fpg_report: -1) */
 
 static WORKERDEF(worker, p)
 {                               /* --- worker function for a thread */
